# WRF v4.6.1 (tag v4.6.1, commit d66e442fccc04111067e29274c9f9eaccc3cef28),
# phys/physics_mmm as that commit carries it.  Every file the gwd_opt = 1
# oracle compiles or cites.  build.sh refuses any other bytes.
#
# bl_gwdo.F90 and module_bl_gwdo.F are byte-identical to WRF v4.7.1's (the
# same sha256 as tools/terrain_drag_wrf471_oracle/SOURCES.sha256), and so is
# the gwdo call in module_pbl_driver.F.  ccpp_kind_types.F differs only in
# its precision guard (4.6.1 '#if ( RWORDSIZE == 4 )', 4.7.1
# '#ifndef DOUBLE_PRECISION'); both make kind_phys real(4) in WRF's default
# single-precision build.
